.TH RASTERLAB 1 "August 2026" "rasterlab 1.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rasterlab \- legacy fixed-point raster container tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rasterlab
.I command
[\fIargs\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Operates on RasterLab raster containers (.rlr). All arithmetic is
integer-only fixed point. Output bytes are deterministic for a given
input and command line.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B info \fIin.rlr\fR
Print container metadata and CRC to stdout.
.TP
.B checksum \fIin.rlr\fR
Print container CRC and per-plane sums to stdout.
.TP
.B convert \-f \fIformat\fR \fIin.rlr\fR \fIout.rlr\fR
Convert between pixel formats. Formats: GRAY8, RGB24, BGR24, RGBA32,
BGRA32, YCC420P, YCC422P, YCC444P (or codes 0-7).
.TP
.B resize \-w \fIwidth\fR \-h \fIheight\fR \-k \fIkernel\fR \fIin.rlr\fR \fIout.rlr\fR
Resample to a new geometry. Kernels: point, tent, cubic4.
Dimensions accepted in [1, 32768].
.TP
.B chain \fIspec\fR \fIin.rlr\fR \fIout.rlr\fR
Apply a semicolon-separated pipeline, e.g.
"convert:RGB24;resize:320x240:tent;convert:YCC420P".
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.TP
.B 3
File cannot be opened or written.
.TP
.B 4
Unsupported format, kernel or dimensions.
.TP
.B 5
Corrupt container.
.SH NOTES
The exact numeric behaviour of colourspace conversion, chroma
subsampling and resampling is defined by the reference implementation,
not by this page. Consult the source.
